{
  "model": "medium",
  "language": "en",
  "text": "Track 4.1 Welcome to Renton and I hope you enjoy your stay here. I'm going to give you some directions so you can find your way around while you are here. We're outside the train station now and in front of us is a historical monument. You can enjoy the sun in our lovely park. It's behind the small shopping centre next to the cafe. There are lots of trees and flowers and a very old fountain in the middle. There is a food court in the shopping centre and you can buy your food here. As you can see, there is a department store opposite the station. Where's the bank? The bank is next to the library. Go down Wood Street, past the museum, turn right and the bank is between the library and the cinema. Where's the university? That's over the river. Walk down Ship Street next to the shopping centre. You can see the river at the end of the street and a bridge to the right. Go over the bridge and the university campus is in front of you. I have maps of the town with me or you can download the app. Renton is a beautiful town and it's very safe too. I hope you enjoy your time here. Thank you.",
